## Architecture provenance

This project's CLI structure, `claude -p` subprocess backend (`src/llm.rs`), loop/gate
logic (`src/loop_run.rs`), and report format (`src/report.rs`) are a port of the
architecture from `Loop-Suite/bizplan-loop` (Apache-2.0), adapted to the ASO domain.

## Ported open-source logic

### semihcihan/App-Store-Optimization-CLI (MIT)
https://github.com/semihcihan/App-Store-Optimization-CLI

`src/checks.rs::normalize_keyword()` / `sanitize_keywords()` / `normalize_text_for_match()`
were rewritten in Rust based on the logic of this repository's `cli/domain/keywords/policy.ts`
(`normalizeKeyword`, `sanitizeKeywords`) and `cli/shared/aso-keyword-utils.ts`
(`normalizeTextForKeywordMatch`). The original TypeScript code was not copied directly —
only the algorithm was ported. The original uses `.normalize("NFKC")` plus a Unicode regex
(`\p{L}\p{N}\p{M}`), but this project approximates it with `char::is_alphanumeric()`
instead of adding the `unicode-normalization` crate (not a full NFKC equivalent — see the
README "Spec" section).

### Repository not referenced

`furkancingoz/aso-skill` has no stated license (NOASSERTION, default copyright protection
applies), so its code was not referenced at all.
